KOREA MINE REHABILITATION AND MINERAL RESOURCES CORPORATION ACT

Article 1 (Purpose)
The purpose of this Act is to contribute to the development of the national economy by establishing the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation to properly manage damage caused by mining and foster and support the mineral resources industry, thereby revitalizing the economy of mining regions and promoting the stable supply of and demand for mineral resources.

Article 2 (Legal personality)
The Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation (hereinafter referred to as the "Corporation") shall be a corporation.

Article 3 (Offices)
(1) The location of the Corporation's principal office shall be prescribed by its articles of incorporation.
(2) If necessary to perform its affairs, the Corporation may establish branches, local offices, offices, or resident representatives at necessary locations in or outside the Republic of Korea following a resolution of its board of directors.

Article 4 (Capital)
The capital of the Corporation shall be three trillion won, all of which shall be contributed by the Government.

Article 5 (Registration)
(1) The Corporation shall be established upon registration of its establishment at the location of its principal office.
(2) Matters concerning registration of establishment of the Corporation under paragraph (1), registration of establishment, relocation, or alteration of branches, local offices, or offices, and other matters necessary for registration of the Corporation shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.
(3) Matters required to be registered by the Corporation shall not be asserted against a third party until such registration has been completed.

Article 6 (Restrictions on the president's authority to represent the Corporation)
Where the interests of the Corporation conflict with those of its president, the president shall not represent the Corporation, and the auditor (or the audit committee, if an audit committee has been established under the Act on the Management of Public Institutions) shall represent the Corporation.

Article 7 (Appointment of agents)
The president may appoint an agent from among the Corporation's employees who is authorized to perform all judicial and extrajudicial acts concerning its affairs, as prescribed by the articles of incorporation.

Article 8 (Projects)
(1) The Corporation shall conduct the following projects to achieve the purposes referred to in Article 1: <Amended on December 30, 2025>
1. Projects for preventing mine damage under Article 11 of the Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage;
2. Formulation of mine damage prevention plans for individual mines and preparation of measures to prevent mine damage;
3. International technical cooperation, international procurement, and official development assistance projects concerning prevention of mine damage;
4. Compensation for damage caused by mining;
5. Projects to improve the environment of mining regions;
6. Guarantees of the performance of debts and other obligations that holders of mining rights or mining concession rights are required to discharge under other Acts;
7. Support for projects specified in Article 29, subparagraphs 1 through 8 of the Coal Industry Act;
8. Projects to revitalize local economies in coal industry transition promotion districts under Article 3 of the Special Act on Support for Development of Coal Industry Transition Regions, and lending projects to foster alternative industries;
9. Investment in and management of corporations (including foreign corporations) that conduct exploration and development of mineral resources (including stone and aggregate resources) and related projects;
10. Management and disposal of overseas investment projects related to mining, and support for private-sector development of mineral resources (including stone and aggregate resources);
11. Loans of funds necessary for the exploration, development, processing, and stockpiling of mineral resources;
12. Stockpiling, trading, and lending of mineral products;
13. Trading and lending of facilities and equipment related to mineral resources;
14. Education, training, technical guidance, and equipment support for mine safety;
15. Collection, use, and management of mineral exploration data;
16. Cooperation projects between South and North Korea concerning development of mineral resources and the mineral resources industry;
17. Services, research, statistical management, informatization, and incidental projects concerning the projects under subparagraphs 1 through 16 and related projects or fields;
18. Other projects entrusted by the State or local governments.
(2) The Minister of Trade and Industry shall determine the items to be stockpiled under paragraph (1) 12, stockpiling methods, and other necessary matters in consultation with the Minister of Finance and Economy. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 9 (Bearing of expenses)
(1) The Corporation may require relevant institutions or beneficiaries to bear expenses necessary for the projects under Article 8 (1), as prescribed by Presidential Decree.
(2) The Corporation may collect fees for projects under Article 8 with approval from the Minister of Trade and Industry. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

Article 10 (Raising funds)
(1) The Corporation shall raise funds necessary for its operation and projects from the following sources:
1. Capital and reserves;
2. Borrowings from within or outside the Republic of Korea;
3. Funds raised through the issuance of bonds under Article 11;
4. Mine damage prevention project funds under Article 22 of the Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage;
5. Income from asset management;
6. Subsidies and contributions under Article 15;
7. Other revenue.
(2) Matters necessary for the management of funds lent under Article 8 (1) 11 shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 11 (Issuance of bonds)
(1) Following a resolution of its board of directors, the Corporation may issue bonds in an amount not exceeding twice the sum of its capital and reserves.
(2) The Government may guarantee repayment of the principal of and interest on bonds issued by the Corporation.
(3) The extinctive prescription for bonds shall be completed five years for principal and two years for interest, calculated from the date the relevant amount becomes repayable.
(4) Other matters necessary for issuance of bonds shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 12 (Disposition of profits and losses)
(1) If profits arise from the settlement of accounts for a business year, the Corporation shall dispose of them in the following order:
1. Coverage of losses carried forward;
2. Accumulation of at least 20 percent of profits as an earned surplus reserve until the amount reaches half of the capital;
3. Accumulation of at least 20 percent of profits as a business expansion reserve until the amount reaches the amount of the capital;
4. Payment into the National Treasury.
(2) If losses arise from the settlement of accounts for a business year, the Corporation shall cover them from the business expansion reserve under paragraph (1) 3; if that reserve is insufficient, from the earned surplus reserve under paragraph (1) 2; and if the latter reserve is still insufficient, the Government may cover the remaining amount.
(3) Earned surplus reserves under paragraph (1) 2 and business expansion reserves under paragraph (1) 3 may be transferred to capital as prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Article 13 (Establishment of overseas assets account)
(1) The Corporation shall establish an overseas assets account, separate from its own accounts, to efficiently dispose of assets, liabilities, and other items arising from overseas resource development conducted by the former Korea Resources Corporation established under the Korea Resources Corporation Act.
(2) Notwithstanding other Acts, the overseas assets account under paragraph (1) shall be accounted for separately from the Corporation's accounts. No funds may be transferred from another account into the overseas assets account or from the overseas assets account into another account.
(3) Funds for the overseas assets account shall be raised by the following means:
1. Capital contributions or subsidies;
2. Borrowings from within or outside the Republic of Korea;
3. Funds raised through issuance of bonds under Article 11;
4. Revenue of the overseas assets account.
(4) Funds of the overseas assets account shall be used for the following purposes:
1. Payment of funds necessary for projects of the overseas assets account or repayment of liabilities;
2. Funding for the creation, operation, and management of the overseas assets account;
3. Other purposes prescribed by Presidential Decree as necessary for projects of the overseas assets account.

Article 14 (Restrictions on disposal of resources for support of coal industry transition regions)
The Corporation shall not sell, lend, or provide as security the following resources for supporting economic revitalization of coal industry transition regions for purposes of operating the overseas assets account or managing liabilities: <Amended on December 30, 2025>
1. Shares in corporations in which the Corporation has invested to revitalize the economy of coal industry transition regions, and dividends on those shares;
2. The Coal Hall established to provide scholarships to children of coal mine workers, and income from its operation;
3. Loan resources for fostering alternative industries in coal industry transition promotion districts;
4. Assets acquired as part of projects to promote former closed-mine regions, including the former Korea Coal Corporation training-center site.

Article 15 (Subsidies and contributions)
(1) The Government may grant subsidies for the Corporation's projects within the budget.
(2) The Government may make contributions to the Corporation from the Special Account for Energy and Resources Projects or the general account for the following expenses:
1. Part of operating expenses;
2. Expenses necessary for research on mine damage prevention and technology development;
3. Part of the expenses necessary to implement mine damage prevention projects concerning operating mines, suspended mines, and closed mines under mine damage prevention implementation plans under Article 8 of the Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage;
4. Expenses necessary to implement mine damage prevention projects concerning the following mines:
(a) Coal industry rationalization mines closed under Article 39-2 of the Coal Industry Act;
(b) Closed metal and non-metal mines for which no person is responsible for causing mine damage;
5. Expenses necessary to compensate for damage arising from the implementation of mine damage prevention projects entrusted under Article 12 of the Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage;
6. Expenses necessary to implement emergency mine damage prevention projects under Article 17 of that Act;
7. Expenses necessary to compensate for losses under Article 19 (5) of that Act;
8. Expenses necessary for projects guaranteeing performance of obligations under Article 8 (1) 6;
9. Expenses necessary for international technical cooperation, international procurement, and official development assistance projects related to mine damage prevention.

Article 16 (Tax support)
Tax reductions and other forms of support may be provided to the Corporation as prescribed by relevant Acts.

Article 17 (Inspection of relevant documents)
(1) Where necessary to conduct any project under Article 8 (1), the Corporation may request registry offices, relevant administrative agencies, or other persons to allow the inspection or copying of documents and other relevant materials or to provide other necessary cooperation.
(2) A person requested to provide materials or take similar action under paragraph (1) shall comply unless there is a compelling reason not to do so.

Article 18 (Prohibition of use of similar names)
No person other than the Corporation established under this Act shall use the name "Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation," "Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation," "Korea Resources Corporation," or any similar name.

Article 19 (Prohibition of disclosure of secrets)
No current or former officer or employee of the Corporation shall disclose or misappropriate secrets learned in the course of performing their duties.

Article 20 (Supervision)
The Minister of Trade and Industry shall guide and supervise the Corporation's affairs in relation to the following matters: <Amended on October 1, 2025>
1. Appropriate performance of projects under Article 8;
2. Projects entrusted to the Corporation by the Minister of Trade and Industry;
3. Proper management and operation of the overseas assets account established under Article 13;
4. Other matters prescribed by other statutes.

Article 21 (Relationship with other Acts)
Matters concerning the organization and management of the Corporation not provided in this Act shall be governed by the Act on the Management of Public Institutions.

Article 22 (Penalties)
A person who discloses or misappropriates secrets in violation of Article 19 shall be punished by imprisonment for not more than two years or by a fine not exceeding 20 million won.

Article 23 (Administrative fines)
(1) A person who uses the name "Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation," "Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation," "Korea Resources Corporation," or any similar name in violation of Article 18 shall be subject to an administrative fine not exceeding five million won.
(2) Administrative fines under paragraph (1) shall be imposed and collected by the Minister of Trade and Industry. <Amended on October 1, 2025>

ADDENDA <Act No. 17919, March 9, 2021>

Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation: Provided, That Article 3 of these Addenda shall enter into force on the date of promulgation.

Article 2 (Repeal of another Act)
The Korea Resources Corporation Act shall be repealed.

Article 3 (Establishment of the Corporation Establishment Committee)
(1) A Corporation Establishment Committee (hereinafter referred to as the "Establishment Committee") shall be established to handle the dissolution of the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation under the former Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation") and the Korea Resources Corporation under the former Korea Resources Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Resources Corporation"), the establishment of and contributions to the Corporation, and other related affairs.
(2) The Establishment Committee shall consist of not more than 15 members. The Vice Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy shall serve as its chairperson, and its members shall be commissioned by the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy. Public officials, heads of headquarters of the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation, and persons with extensive knowledge and experience in mine damage management and mineral resources shall participate as members.
(3) The Establishment Committee shall prepare the articles of incorporation of the Corporation and obtain authorization from the Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy.
(4) The Establishment Committee shall register the establishment of the Corporation without delay after its officers are appointed.
(5) Upon completion of registration of establishment under paragraph (4), the Establishment Committee shall hand over its affairs to the president of the Corporation without delay; when the handover is completed, the Establishment Committee shall be deemed dissolved and its members shall be deemed dismissed or released from their commissions.
(6) The Establishment Committee may receive support for expenses necessary to prepare for the establishment of the Corporation within the budgets of the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation.

[Effective date: March 9, 2021] Article 3

Article 4 (Special cases concerning dissolution and liquidation)
The Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation shall be deemed dissolved simultaneously with the establishment of the Corporation under this Act, notwithstanding the provisions of the Civil Act concerning dissolution and liquidation.

Article 5 (General transitional measures)
Dispositions, procedures, and other acts conducted under the former Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage and the Korea Resources Corporation Act at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed conducted under this Act insofar as they do not conflict with this Act.

Article 6 (Succession to rights and obligations)
(1) Upon its establishment, the Corporation shall comprehensively succeed to all property, claims, debts, and other rights and obligations belonging to the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation.
(2) The names of the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation recorded in registries, other official documents, and books concerning property, rights, and obligations succeeded to under paragraph (1) shall be deemed replaced with the name of the Corporation simultaneously with its establishment.
(3) The value of property succeeded to by the Corporation shall be the book value as of the day preceding the date of its establishment, finalized through due diligence on assets and other relevant items.

Article 7 (Measures concerning officers and employees)
(1) Upon the establishment of the Corporation, the terms of office of the officers of the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation shall be deemed to have expired.
(2) Upon the establishment of the Corporation, persons employed by the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation at that time shall be deemed employees of the Corporation.

Article 8 (Transitional measures concerning Government contributions)
Property contributed by the Government to the Korea Resources Corporation under the former Korea Resources Corporation Act at the time this Act enters into force shall be deemed contributed to the Corporation.

Article 9 (Transitional measures concerning projects of the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation)
Projects conducted or being conducted by the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation and the Korea Resources Corporation before this Act enters into force shall be deemed projects conducted or being conducted by the Corporation.

Article 10 (Transitional measures for disposal of overseas assets)
(1) The Corporation shall manage and dispose of assets arising from mineral-related projects conducted overseas by the Korea Resources Corporation (hereinafter referred to as "overseas assets" in this Article) as determined by the Overseas Assets Management Committee under paragraph (2). In such cases, the Korea Asset Management Corporation established under the Act on the Establishment of the Korea Asset Management Corporation shall act as agent for sales of overseas assets.
(2) An Overseas Assets Management Committee shall be established within the Ministry of Trade and Industry to comprehensively deliberate on and resolve matters concerning disposal of overseas assets under paragraph (1). <Amended on October 1, 2025>
(3) The Overseas Assets Management Committee shall consist of the following persons, and its chairperson shall be a person elected from among the members: <Amended on October 1, 2025>
1. Two experts in economics recommended by the competent standing committee of the National Assembly and commissioned by the Minister of Trade and Industry;
2. Five experts in sales of overseas mineral resource investment assets prescribed by Presidential Decree and designated by the Minister of Trade and Industry.
(4) Meetings of the Overseas Assets Management Committee shall open with the attendance of a majority of all members and adopt resolutions with the affirmative votes of a majority of members present. Proceedings of the Committee shall be recorded stenographically.
(5) If necessary for deliberation and resolution under paragraph (2), the Committee may demand that the Corporation submit related data or may conduct on-site investigations of relevant institutions.
(6) None of the following persons may become a member referred to in any subparagraph of paragraph (3), and requirements concerning the expertise needed to qualify as a member shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree:
1. A person who is not a national of the Republic of Korea;
2. A person who falls under any subparagraph of Article 33 of the State Public Officials Act.
(7) A secretariat shall be established within the Ministry of Trade and Industry to assist the Committee in its affairs and provide practical support, and matters necessary for its organization and operation shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree. <Amended on October 1, 2025>
(8) Article 8 (1) 9 shall remain effective until all overseas assets are sold.

Article 11 (Transitional measures concerning penalties)
The former Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage and the Korea Resources Corporation Act shall apply to criminal penalties and administrative fines for acts committed before this Act enters into force.

Article 12 (Amendments to other Acts)
(1) Part of the Mine Safety Act shall be amended as follows:

In Article 22-4 (2), "the Korea Resources Corporation under the Korea Resources Corporation Act or the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation under the Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage" shall be replaced with "the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation under the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act".

(2) Part of the Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage shall be amended as follows:

Article 12 (2) 1 shall be replaced with the following:

1. The Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation under the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the "Corporation").

Article 23 (1) 6 shall be replaced with the following:

6. Operation of the Corporation.

In Article 30 (2), "the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation under Article 31" shall be replaced with "the Corporation".

Chapter VII (Articles 31 through 43) shall be deleted.

Article 45 shall be deleted.

Article 47, subparagraph 4 shall be deleted.

Article 49 shall be deleted.

(3) Part of the Coal Industry Act shall be amended as follows:

In Article 27 (1) 5, "the Korea Resources Corporation under the Korea Resources Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the 'Korea Resources Corporation')" shall be replaced with "the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation under the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act (hereinafter referred to as the 'Corporation')".

In Article 28 (1) 5, "Korea Resources Corporation" shall be replaced with "Corporation".

In the part of Article 39-3 (1) other than its subparagraphs, "the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation under Article 31 of the Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage (hereinafter referred to as the 'Corporation')" shall be replaced with "the Corporation".

(4) Part of the Restriction of Special Local Taxation Act shall be amended as follows:

In Article 62 (3), "the Korea Resources Corporation established under the Korea Resources Corporation Act" shall be replaced with "the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation established under the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act".

Article 13 (Relationship with other statutes)
(1) Where other statutes in force at the time this Act enters into force cite the former Act on the Prevention and Restoration of Mine Damage or the Korea Resources Corporation Act, or any provision thereof, and this Act has a corresponding provision, the citation shall be deemed a citation of this Act or the corresponding provision hereof.
(2) Where other statutes in force at the time this Act enters into force cite the Korea Mine Reclamation Corporation or the Korea Resources Corporation, the citation shall be deemed a citation of the Corporation under this Act.

ADDENDA (Government Organization Act) <Act No. 21065, October 1, 2025>

Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation: Provided, That portions of Acts amended under Article 7 of these Addenda that were promulgated before this Act enters into force but whose enforcement dates have not yet arrived shall enter into force on the respective dates on which those Acts enter into force; and the following amended provisions shall enter into force on the dates specified in the relevant subparagraphs:

1. The following amended provisions shall enter into force on January 2, 2026: Provided, That portions of Acts amended under Article 7 of these Addenda (limited to portions related to the amendments in items (a) and (b)) that were promulgated before the enforcement date under the main sentence of this subparagraph but whose enforcement dates under that sentence have not yet arrived shall enter into force on the respective dates on which those Acts enter into force:
(a) Amended provisions of Article 19 (4), Article 23, Article 29 (1) 1, and Article 30;
(b) Amended provisions of Article 12 (2), Article 19 (3), Article 22, and the proviso of Article 29 (2) (limited to the portions concerning the Minister of Finance and Economy and the Ministry of Finance and Economy);
(c) Acts amended under Article 7 of these Addenda (limited to portions related to the amended provisions in items (a) and (b)).
2. Omitted.

Articles 2 through 6 Omitted.

Article 7 (Amendments to other Acts)
(1) through (288) Omitted.

(289) Part of the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act shall be amended as follows:

In Article 8 (2), "Minister of Economy and Finance" shall be replaced with "Minister of Finance and Economy".

In Article 8 (2), Article 9 (2), the part of Article 20 other than its subparagraphs, subparagraph 2 of that Article, Article 23 (2), and Article 10 (3) 1 and 2 of the Addenda, "Minister of Trade, Industry and Energy" shall be replaced with "Minister of Trade and Industry", respectively.

In Article 10 (2) and (7) of the Addenda, "Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy" shall be replaced with "Ministry of Trade and Industry", respectively.

(290) through (626) Omitted.

Article 8 Omitted.

ADDENDA (Special Act on Support for Development of Coal Industry Transition Regions) <Act No. 21254, December 30, 2025>

Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force three months after the date of its promulgation. <Proviso omitted>

Article 2 (Amendments to other Acts)
(1) through (7) Omitted.

(8) Part of the Korea Mine Rehabilitation and Mineral Resources Corporation Act shall be amended as follows:

In Article 8 (1) 8, "promotion district for abandoned mine areas under Article 3 of the Special Act on Support for Development of Abandoned Mine Areas" shall be replaced with "coal industry transition promotion district under Article 3 of the Special Act on Support for Development of Coal Industry Transition Regions".

In the heading of Article 14, "support for abandoned mine areas" shall be replaced with "support for coal industry transition regions"; in the part of that Article other than its subparagraphs, "abandoned mine areas" shall be replaced with "coal industry transition regions"; in subparagraph 1 of that Article, "abandoned mine areas" shall be replaced with "coal industry transition regions"; and in subparagraph 3 of that Article, "abandoned mine areas" shall be replaced with "coal industry transition regions".

(9) Omitted.
